{
  "id": "30741_soukou",
  "headword": "{装甲|そうこう}",
  "reading": "そうこう",
  "romaji": "soukou",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "armour plating; armouring",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "armour; armour plating",
      "explanation": "Protective plating fitted to a vehicle, ship, or aircraft, and by extension the act of fitting it. Used of machines, not of the armour a person wears, which is {鎧|よろい}."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30741_soukou_ex1",
      "japanese": "{装甲|そうこう}が{厚|あつ}い。",
      "english": "The armour is thick.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30741_soukou_ex2",
      "japanese": "{現金|げんきん}を{運|はこ}ぶのは{装甲|そうこう}された{車両|しゃりょう}だ。",
      "english": "Cash is transported in armoured vehicles.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30741_soukou_ex3",
      "japanese": "この{戦車|せんしゃ}は{装甲|そうこう}を{強化|きょうか}した{分|ぶん}、{重|おも}くなって{速度|そくど}が{落|お}ちた。",
      "english": "This tank's armour was reinforced, but it became heavier and slower as a result.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{装|そう} (to fit, to equip) + {甲|こう} (shell, carapace).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {装甲車|そうこうしゃ}: an armoured vehicle\n- {装甲|そうこう}が{厚|あつ}い / {薄|うす}い: thickly / thinly armoured\n- {装甲|そうこう}を{強化|きょうか}する: to reinforce the armour\n- {重|じゅう}{装甲|そうこう}: heavy armour\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {鎧|よろい}: armour worn on the body — the samurai or knight kind\n- {防弾|ぼうだん}: bulletproofing — of glass, vests, and the like\n\nOutside military and news contexts, learners meet the word mostly in games and anime, where {重|じゅう}{装甲|そうこう} describes a heavily protected robot or unit.",
